{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/344085-isil-and-the-arisen","id":344085,"title":"ISIL and the Arisen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-18T13:48:20-08:00","id":344085,"title":"ISIL and the Arisen","content":"I'm sorry if this is an uncomfortable or inappropriate topic. Mummy is a modern game though and it takes place in our world, more or less, so I was wondering what people have done to handle recent evolutions in the region with ISIL? It's a topic more relevant to the Arisen than other WoD games as ISIL more or less occupies ancient Irem. Is it possible some shadowy supernatural conspiracy is working against the Arisen through ISIL, or vice-versa? How do modern Arisen view the political situation in ancient Irem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T14:40:44-08:00","id":344116,"title":"","content":"Irem was based in the Nile Delta, wasn't it? I wouldn't go anywhere near as far as &quot;ISIL more or less occupies ancient Irem&quot;. They have several countries to cross before that happens.<br /> <br /> That said, I prefer to imagine that events like what we're witnessing in Iraq and Syria are grounded in humans, not the supernatural. That certainly doesn't prevent the supernatural from exploiting these events, however. There have already been cases of illegal antiquities sales being used to fuel the violence, and that in Mummy almost certainly means that there's an opportunity to snatch up relics. Mummies in the area are probably operating at quite an inconvenience, especially if their cultists are being targeted or tombs being raided for artefacts, while those outside the region with interests inside likely have had a lot of chances win favour with their Judges through the retrieval of relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:27:47-08:00","id":344215,"title":"","content":"It occupies territory implied to fall under the Nameless Empire (the same way Iberia, Gaul, Britain, and Egypt fell under the Roman Empire, but are not Rome). Irem itself was indeed in the Nile Delta, not Mesopotamia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:49:33-08:00","id":344230,"title":"","content":"Sure, I get that. I do see there being a marked difference to most Mummies though between a perceived threat to Irem itself, or at least its ruins (if it left any), and what used to be the provinces. Mummies who did come from those regions may get invested in the struggle for one reason or another, but it doesn't strike me as a conflict that risks the legacy of Irem.<br /> <br /> I see the perception of any Mummy not from that precise region having views not too dissimilar to that of the way an Italian would see a civil war in Britain or France, to use your own example. At least, in the case of those Mummies who were Iremite natives. To those who came from territories on the opposite side of the empire, it would be at an even greater remove.<br /> <br /> &quot;It depends&quot; is pretty much the hallmark of this kind of discussion, but it's particularly relevant in this matter. If this conflict were happening in Egypt in the area where Irem itself once stood, then you might have a far more universal reaction from Arisen. Many modern Arisen might not even remember that Iraq-Syria were parts of the Nameless Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:55:12-08:00","id":344234,"title":"","content":"Given their Memory problems, I\u2019d say that most of the Arisen have only a vague and tentative link to Irem; and they\u2019ve long since migrated all over the world. I see no more reason to link them to ISIL than anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T22:28:36-08:00","id":344378,"title":"","content":"I think that Arisen might well find it easy to relate to the ISIL way of thinking, with them being used to Stone Age sensibilities and all. I could see ISIL cults and pawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:42:57-08:00","id":344437,"title":"","content":"I don't see any more reason for them to be connected to the Arisan than any other. It's a tacky idea, and the whole issue of attributing very human evils to supernatural influence comes to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:55:56-08:00","id":344441,"title":"","content":"Mummies probably can move about more freely in that region right now. Neither the beliefs or actions of that group are new. It has been going on for generations, off and on for centuries. I would expect they are used to it by now. It seems unlikely that mummies would care much about them unless they were personally affected. I guess they might mind the somewhat destabilized nature of the region. Mummies tend towards liking order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:55:47-08:00","id":344650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/344085-isil-and-the-arisen?p=344437#post344437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any more reason for them to be connected to the Arisan than any other. It's a tacky idea, and the whole issue of attributing very human evils to supernatural influence comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not attributing human evil to the Arisen. I'm saying that the Arisen might well find it useful to exploit the preexisting notions and beliefs of certain cultures and scumbags. Slave drivers, people who bury humans alive as gifts to the Judges and people who run gigantic eugenics projects (for reference see Guildhalls of the Deathless), etc. shouldn't really have any sort of problems cooperating with the worst humanity has to offer, and might well that sort of people as being useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T11:18:22-08:00","id":344976,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it mentioned in a couple of books how Islam is a problematic subject for some mummies, given how some Islamic extremists have destroyed ancient places and items that might contain Sekhem (the destruction of the Buddhas of Bamiyan by the Taliban in Afghanistan comes to mind). <br /> <br /> I imagine ISIL might be the same way. A mummy who holds power over a given ISIL battalion or whatever does have a potentially well-armed Cult at his disposal (and almost definitely <i>his</i>, given the attitude towards women that, even if broken by Arisen magic, would still be problematic when dealing with non-Cult ISIL members). The flipside is that a Cult that is comprised of obvious members of ISIL is hardly low-key and actively being targeted by a number of enemies ranging from Assad's Syrian army to the Turkish Peshmerga to the varied organs of the United States, EU, and Israel military and intelligence communities.<br /> <br /> There's also the question of what kind of goals a mummy leading an ISIL cult hopes to achieve. Mummies are not designed to rule openly (and suffer quicker degeneration for doing so - they're mighty servants, not pharaohs) and ISIL's goal is establishing a fundamental caliphate in the region. Having an armed military Cult might help them forcibly seize Relics and advance their personal agendas in conquered areas, but again there's the trade-off of huge visibility that is much more problematic than if your Cult is formed as a corporation or even a hidden conspiracy. And, with that region in particular, I wouldn't be surprised if you're going to make enemies of local Arisen whose own Cults are groups that are now being persecuted by ISIL - the Yazidis, for example, or former Iraqi or Syrian elites toppled from power in the area by ISIL's conquests who will want to drive them out and will call upon their patrons for help and support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T15:19:49-08:00","id":345172,"title":"","content":"I think Zeibinnean is on to something. The Arisen cults are going to be the ones being persecuted. If any Mummies are involved with IS, I'd have it be along the lines of a conspiracy cult; pretending to be a sympathetic foreign backer in order to secure relics in return for resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:13:01-08:00","id":345831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/344085-isil-and-the-arisen?p=345172#post345172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Zeibinnean is on to something. The Arisen cults are going to be the ones being persecuted. If any Mummies are involved with IS, I'd have it be along the lines of a conspiracy cult; pretending to be a sympathetic foreign backer in order to secure relics in return for resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've owned the Deceived book since it came out but am only now getting down to reading it in detail. If anything, I could see a branch of ISIL (not the whole organization probably, but one group under its overall command structure) as being a Deceived Cult. The apparent fundamentalism and brutal nihilism really seem like they could apply. Particularly for the Musician or the Keeper.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if another section of the organization is actually under the power of an Arisen, trying to use the repressive culture to take control of areas and wrest Relics from them, with the Deceived aware of the Arisen but not vice versa. Vipers wearing the guise of fellows-in-arms...<br /> <br /> Could be a hell of a basis for a game. Especially considering how good Arisen might be at becoming the center of a Cult. I have a Mummy whose Cult is the students (and eventual alumni) of an Ivy League Secret Society, who wind up having all kinds of legit and shady connections in government agencies. Not a stretch for a Mummy to take a CIA service post as his cult, or a Mossad cell, or whatever, especially with a friend in DC or Tel Aviv who can pull strings for assignments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}